-`--sort` and `--direction` select the ordering column and direction; both default
-to a timestamp descending sort. Results are unpaginated.
+Options:
 
-Clause building lives in `auditlog.filters`, so the same escaping and ordering
+- `--actor` (required): actor to match.
+- `--action`: action to match. Omit it to match every action for the actor.
+- `--since`: only rows at or after an ISO 8601 date or datetime, e.g. `2026-01-31`.
+- `--sort`: column to order by: `id`, `actor`, `action`, `target` or `ts` (default `ts`).
+- `--direction`: `asc` or `desc` (default `desc`).
+- `--limit`: maximum rows to return, 1 to 1000 (default 50).
+- `--offset`: rows to skip (default 0).
+
+Ties in the sort column are broken by `id`, so pages are stable.
+
+Clause building lives in `auditlog.filters`, so the same allowlist and ordering
 rules apply to every query against the table.
